  "sources": [
    {
      "kind": "datasheet",
      "url": "https://assets.ctfassets.net/4zjnzn055a4v/1qUiHwGHNmumKgYugG6wws/837b26c2261771b9d58a94c44bb1cdc4/8030c_views.pdf",
      "note": "Genelec 8030C dimension drawing 8030C_views (opened, rendered): 299 mm overall height incl. Iso-Pod, 189 mm wide, 178 mm deep, acoustic axis 190 mm, Iso-Pod offset 15 mm, M6 depth 10 holes 76 mm apart. The rear view (drawing rotated 90 degrees on the page) was re-rendered upright at 5.67 px/mm (checked on the 299 mm height and the 76 mm M6 spacing): the amplifier plate is 118.6 mm wide and centred, the square power button at the plate centre line (10 x 10 mm, 134.9 mm above the base of the Iso-Pod). In that drawing the cabinet outline measures about 174 mm across against the 189 mm spec width (unexplained), so only positions relative to the centre line and the vertical scale were used; expect +/- 3 mm on the power button."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://images.ctfassets.net/4zjnzn055a4v/24f3PvLYfkiyxYYq14xMzp/96fd447157086fbc543f46dc40e74d94/8030CP-k10_web.jpg",
      "note": "Genelec 8030C rear/underside product photo (opened, 900 px wide): the connector panel is a horizontal strip below the amplifier plate, facing down: IEC inlet on the left, XLR input on the right (seen from behind), a small screw between them. Scale 3.08 px/mm from the plate width (365 px = 118.6 mm); offsets from the plate centre line (px 452): IEC -36.4 mm, XLR +42.2 mm. y = 107 mm is the height of that strip in the upright rear drawing (about 1190 px of the rendered crop, 5.67 px/mm, 1795 px at the base of the Iso-Pod). Oblique view: expect +/- 6 mm."
    },
    {
      "kind": "manual",
      "url": "https://assets.ctfassets.net/4zjnzn055a4v/1my4dzvqUoe4oKYwS6KsUu/a8f964c3ce07eb802b88b8d861799a07/8030c_opman_gb_fi.pdf",
      "note": "Genelec 8030C operating manual (opened, text read, p.5 figure rendered): Figure 3 'Control and connector layout on the rear panel' (reflex port, threads, tone controls, sensitivity adjustment, power switch, horizontal connector panel, Iso-Pod); specification table: height 299 mm with Iso-Pod (285 mm without), width 189 mm, depth 178 mm, weight 5.0 kg, XLR female balanced input."
    },
    {
      "kind": "datasheet",
      "url": "https://www.neutrik.com/en/product/nc3md-l-1",
      "note": "Neutrik NC3MD-L-1 product page (opened): \"Standardized D sized 24 mm panel cutout\". openingMm = 24 for the XLR input is a guess by that convention (the photo ring is about 22.7 mm)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://images.ctfassets.net/4zjnzn055a4v/37Yluwn69OLB2BOtk0fYTl/d7ac8755a4ad5b397d1ccfff6d8b8eb8/8030CP-k01.jpg",
      "note": "Genelec 8030CP straight-on front photo (2000 x 2000 px, opened, silhouette profiled row by row with the rear photo 8030_Back.jpg): the product is 985 px wide at its widest for 189 mm (5.21 px/mm) and its sides are a shallow arc in elevation, 175 mm wide 39 mm below the top, 189 mm at about 140 mm below the top and 172 mm at 250 mm below it, so the curved-cabinet params barrelMm 17.7 (half-width lost at the far end of the height, a parabola) centred at 159 mm above the base. The woofer grille measures 715 px = 137 mm across (ring 136 mm) with its centre 184 mm below the top of the body = 115 mm above the base; the tweeter ring 216 px = 41 mm, centre 66 mm below the top = 233 mm above the base. The picture of the front is this photo cropped to the body (501,195,985,1475 px, the Iso-Pod mostly cut), the rear picture 8030_Back.jpg cropped to (492,180,1068,1600); white corners are filled (--project-photo ...,fill). Plan radii (front 20, rear 26 mm), the plan taper (rear polygon 172 mm) and the 14 mm Iso-Pod pad (118 x 100 mm) are estimates read off the three-quarter photos; the side and top faces carry no picture."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.genelec.com/8030c",
      "note": "Wave 5 re-measure on the rear picture (rear.jpg crop 492,180,1068,1600 over 189 x 299 mm, read on a mm grid): the ANALOG IN XLR symbol centre is (135.9, 65.2), the first position (137.3, 70) sat 4.9 mm above it; the mains inlet is not visible on the photo (only its MAINS INPUT label), so power-in is kept. +/- 1 mm."
    }
